# The build context is tarred and uploaded to the Docker daemon, which in the
# reference environment lives in a VirtualBox VM across a TLS connection — so
# context size costs time on every single build. node_modules is ~84 MB of an
# ~85 MB context, and `npm ci` recreates it inside the image anyway.
# See docs/architecture.md#docker-machine--virtualbox-on-windows
node_modules/

# Build output. The image produces its own dist/ in the builder stage; copying a
# Windows-built one in would defeat the point of building in the image.
dist/

# Local tooling output.
coverage/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log

# Not used by the image build. Note that nginx.conf IS used — do not add it.
README.md
.gitignore

# Editors / IDEs
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
